\\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $f_1$, $f_2$, $f_3$, $\\dots$ be a sequence of numbers such that\n\\[\n  f_n = f_{n - 1} + f_{n - 2}\n\\]for every integer $n \\ge 3$.  If $f_7 = 83$, what is the sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence?\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nTo solve for the sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence \\( f_1, f_2, f_3, \\ldots \\) defined by the recurrence relation \\( f_n = f_{n-1} + f_{n-2} \\) for \\( n \\geq 3 \\), and given that \\( f_7 = 83 \\), we need to determine the values of \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\) first.\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"Continue from the interruption. Output only the continuation. Do not restart the solution.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"dff9e2cde178d4bc73d04b92cade011eec17441afb46a933d4ecf660b5b37e9a"},"seconds":54.335477352142334,"seed":271581826417444706,"stop":"eos","text":"To proceed, we first express the terms of the sequence in terms of \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nf_3 & = f_2 + f_1, \\\\\nf_4 & = f_3 + f_2 = (f_2 + f_1) + f_2 = f_1 + 2f_2, \\\\\nf_5 & = f_4 + f_3 = (f_1 + 2f_2) + (f_2 + f_1) = 2f_1 + 3f_2, \\\\\nf_6 & = f_5 + f_4 = (2f_1 + 3f_2) + (f_1 + 2f_2) = 3f_1 + 5f_2, \\\\\nf_7 & = f_6 + f_5 = (3f_1 + 5f_2) + (2f_1 + 3f_2) = 5f_1 + 8f_2.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nGiven that \\( f_7 = 83 \\), we have:\n\n\\[\n5f_1 + 8f_2 = 83.\n\\]\n\nWe need to find integer solutions for \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\). Trying possible values for \\( f_1 \\) and solving for \\( f_2 \\):\n\nIf \\( f_1 = 5 \\):\n\n\\[\n5(5) + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 25 + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 8f_2 = 58 \\implies f_2 = 7.25,\n\\]\n\nwhich is not an integer. Trying another value:\n\nIf \\( f_1 = 3 \\):\n\n\\[\n5(3) + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 15 + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 8f_2 = 68 \\implies f_2 = 8.5,\n\\]\n\nwhich is not an integer. Trying another value:\n\nIf \\( f_1 = 1 \\):\n\n\\[\n5(1) + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 5 + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 8f_2 = 78 \\implies f_2 = 9.75,\n\\]\n\nwhich is not an integer. Trying another value:\n\nIf \\( f_1 = 7 \\):\n\n\\[\n5(7) + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 35 + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 8f_2 = 48 \\implies f_2 = 6,\n\\]\n\nwhich is an integer. Thus, \\( f_1 = 7 \\) and \\( f_2 = 6 \\).\n\nNow, we can calculate the sum of the first 10 terms:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nf_1 & = 7, \\\\\nf_2 & = 6, \\\\\nf_3 & = 13, \\\\\nf_4 & = 19, \\\\\nf_5 & = 32, \\\\\nf_6 & = 51, \\\\\nf_7 & = 83, \\\\\nf_8 & = 134, \\\\\nf_9 & = 217, \\\\\nf_{10} & = 351.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nSumming these terms:\n\n\\[\n7 + 6 + 13 + 19 + 32 + 51 + 83 + 134 + 217 + 351 = 913.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence is \\(\\boxed{913}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{913}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To proceed, we first express the terms of the sequence in terms of \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nf_3 & = f_2 + f_1, \\\\\nf_4 & = f_3 + f_2 = (f_2 + f_1) + f_2 = f_1 + 2f_2, \\\\\nf_5 & = f_4 + f_3 = (f_1 + 2f_2) + (f_2 + f_1) = 2f_1 + 3f_2, \\\\\nf_6 & = f_5 + f_4 = (2f_1 + 3f_2) + (f_1 + 2f_2) = 3f_1 + 5f_2, \\\\\nf_7 & = f_6 + f_5 = (3f_1 + 5f_2) + (2f_1 + 3f_2) = 5f_1 + 8f_2.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nGiven that \\( f_7 = 83 \\), we have:\n\n\\[\n5f_1 + 8f_2 = 83.\n\\]\n\nWe need to find integer solutions for \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\). Trying possible values for \\( f_1 \\) and solving for \\( f_2 \\):\n\nIf \\( f_1 = 5 \\):\n\n\\[\n5(5) + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 25 + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 8f_2 = 58 \\implies f_2 = 7.25,\n\\]\n\nwhich is not an integer. Trying another value:\n\nIf \\( f_1 = 3 \\):\n\n\\[\n5(3) + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 15 + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 8f_2 = 68 \\implies f_2 = 8.5,\n\\]\n\nwhich is not an integer. Trying another value:\n\nIf \\( f_1 = 1 \\):\n\n\\[\n5(1) + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 5 + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 8f_2 = 78 \\implies f_2 = 9.75,\n\\]\n\nwhich is not an integer. Trying another value:\n\nIf \\( f_1 = 7 \\):\n\n\\[\n5(7) + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 35 + 8f_2 = 83 \\implies 8f_2 = 48 \\implies f_2 = 6,\n\\]\n\nwhich is an integer. Thus, \\( f_1 = 7 \\) and \\( f_2 = 6 \\).\n\nNow, we can calculate the sum of the first 10 terms:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nf_1 & = 7, \\\\\nf_2 & = 6, \\\\\nf_3 & = 13, \\\\\nf_4 & = 19, \\\\\nf_5 & = 32, \\\\\nf_6 & = 51, \\\\\nf_7 & = 83, \\\\\nf_8 & = 134, \\\\\nf_9 & = 217, \\\\\nf_{10} & = 351.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nSumming these terms:\n\n\\[\n7 + 6 + 13 + 19 + 32 + 51 + 83 + 134 + 217 + 351 = 913.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence is \\(\\boxed{913}\\).","id":"intermediate_algebra:573"}
